  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "authentication",
      "title": "What attestation proves",
      "items": [
        "The attested path verifies Apple evidence, challenge freshness and expected device identity before admission policy. Unattested issuance requires an explicit configured exception.",
        "Finalization checks the CSR signature, reverifies stored attestation against the CSR key, and rechecks admission. Accepting a challenge does not itself issue a certificate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "policy",
      "title": "Protocol and policy",
      "items": [
        "Signed requests use one-use replay nonces. Identifier HMAC verification is stateless; the new-order transaction claims the identifier once while creating protocol state.",
        "Issuance persists a CSR-bound certificate receipt under the order lock before registration. Retries reuse that certificate; required registration must complete before the certificate is exposed.",
        "Finalize retries and order polls can recover pending registration after key, expiry and policy rechecks. Certificate retrieval checks account ownership and refuses incomplete registration.",
        "ACME protocol failures use problem documents. Optional issuance registration and revocation add certificate-status tracking."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "transport",
      "title": "Public documentation",
      "items": [
        "ACMECertificate — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicemanagement/acmecertificate",
        "Deploy Managed Device Attestation — https://support.apple.com/en-gb/guide/deployment/dep54e5ac1fd/web",
        "RFC 8555 — ACME — https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8555",
        "Validate Managed Device Attestation — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicemanagement/validating-a-managed-device-attestation-attestation"
      ]
    },
    {
